hreshold at `simulate_holistic_nav.py:913`, `etf_frac=0.70` from `PARK_STATES`, `_etf_day_cap`, FIFO, `×0.99`) already embedded in the pinned backtest, not re-tuned.", "capacity_adv_realism": "fail — read `_etf_day_cap()` at `simulate_holistic_nav.py:440-446`: it is `etf_liquidity_pct × etf_adv_lookup.get(today)`, i.e. calibrated to **E1VFVN30 ETF's own ADV**, not to the ADV of the 30 discrete equities in the live [REDACTED]V basket. Section B2/B4 proposes reusing this exact cap verbatim as the live per-session trim ceiling ('không đặt trần %/phiên mới... `_etf_day_cap` đã có sẵn') while simultaneously acknowledging (B4) that live PARK is '30 mã riêng lẻ' vs the engine's pooled-ETF abstraction — but never reconciles that the liquidity ceiling itself, not just the trim ORDER, was pooled-ETF-shaped. Applying an ETF-ADV-sized VND cap to trims spread across up to 30 individual (some potentially illiquid) value names risks breaching per-name %ADV even while staying under the aggregate cap.", "arithmetic_mechanism": "pass — verified the '6/13 years C beats A' sub-claim by hand from the raw annual tables: C > A in exactly 2016, 2017, 2019, 2020, 2022, 2025 (6 years) — exact match to the doc's named years. `w_lag_current=0.495`/`alloc_note='as of [REDACTED]'`/`band_breach=false`/`n_park=30`/`park_rebal_date=2026-05-05`/`etf_park_frac=0.7` all reproduced byte-for-byte from `data/golive_v23_status.json`. `deferred_total_with_fee_vnd=171,096,626`, `available_cash_vnd=4,821,143`, `orders=[]` and the literal deferred_reason text reproduced from `data/trade_plans/plan_[REDACTED]_[REDACTED].json`. `totalCash=14,596,244` reproduced from `dnse_raw_[REDACTED]03.jsonl`. Mechanism claims (allocator is post-hoc scalar accounting, not order-generating; DT5G is untouched by this whole topic) are consistent with code."}, "independent_recompute": "Recomputed IS/OOS geometric CAGR from the raw per-year sys-return series in v2_A_control.log and v2_C_skip.log: got A_IS=27.04%, C_IS=25.43%, A_OOS=30.15%, C_OOS=30.29% — matches the finding's C3 table to the basis point. Also reproduced md5 clustering (v1 3-way tie, v2 3-way distinct with A==production), the 6/13-year win count, and every cited field in golive_v23_status.json / plan_[REDACTED]_[REDACTED].json / dnse_raw_[REDACTED]03.jsonl exactly.", "killer_objection": "The proposed L1/L2 trim cap (`_etf_day_cap`) is derived from E1VFVN30 ETF ADV, not from the ADV of the 30 individual [REDACTED]V names that live would actually be trimming — the design reuses a pooled-liquidity number for a fundamentally different (per-name, possibly less liquid) execution surface without checking the reconciliation. This is a real, unaddressed capacity risk in section B (not yet wired), distinct from the otherwise well-substantiated diagnostic finding.", "recommended_reruns": ["Before implementing L1/L2: pull per-ticker `Trading_Value_1M_P50`/ADV for the current 30-name [REDACTED]V basket and compare against the VND size a single day's `_etf_day_cap()` would authorize a trim of, split pro-rata across names — confirm no single name's implied trim exceeds a sane %ADV.", "Run the promised 4th ablation leg (disable block 4c / PREFILL_STATE_REBAL) to isolate L1's standalone contribution, as the doc itself flags as outstanding.", "Complete the P0 book/play_type-at-fill journal tagging (A7 blocker) before computing any live `park_mv_live`, since the current name-based inference is already known to misclassify at least one live position (VPB tagged 'LAG/PARK')."], "summary": "This is an unusually well-evidenced finding — I independently retraced nearly every specific claim (code line numbers, md5 hashes, JSON field values, DNSE balance figures, plan-file deferred amounts, and a from-scratch IS/OOS CAGR recompute from the raw annual-return logs) and every one matched exactly, including the self-critical parts (the v1-ablation-was-a-no-op correction, and the OOS-near-zero/LOO-2023-carries-it-all caveat that correctly bars citing +0.7